 tree in the mulberry family of Moraceae. Native to India, the species was first described under the name Artocarpus heterophyllus in Encyclopédie Méthodique, Botanique in 1789 by Jean-Baptiste Lamarck, based on a specimen collected by botanist Philibert Commerson."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-jackfruit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackfruit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"]]],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Gudeg","dish/gudeg"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bay leaf","ingredient/bay-leaf"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Gnetum gnemon","ingredient/gnetum-gnemon"],["Nangka","ingredient/nangka"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Red onion","ingredient/red-onion"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tempeh","ingredient/tempeh"],["Garcinia binucao","ingredient/garcinia-binucao"],["Pigeon pea","ingredient/pigeon-pea"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/3/3b/The_jackfruit_is_holding_on_to_the_tree.jpg/500px-The_jackfruit_is_holding_on_to_the_tree.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"This work was made by Tushar Hossain and released under the license(s) stated below.…","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_jackfruit_is_holding_on_to_the_tree.jpg"}},"dish/hash-stew":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hash-stew","n":"Hash (stew)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Southern American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Hash, often called pork hash or liver hash, is a name for a stew or gravy made of pork, offal and onions. It is usually paired with rice as \"hash and rice\". Hash is part of the cuisine of the Southern United States where it was invented as a way to use unappetizing cuts of meat. The dish is primarily consumed within the state of South Carolina, where it is commonly paired with barbecue. Many variations of hash exist, which include different combinations of meats and vegetables."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hash-stew"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hash_(stew)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Southern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-southern-united-states"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Lana's Cooking","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lanascooking.com","note":"Lana Stuart's blog of Southern home cooking from Georgia.","url":"https://www.lanascooking.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"A Southern Soul: Southern Classics","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"asouthernsoul.com","note":"Collection of classic Southern recipes on a Southern home cooking blog.","url":"https://asouthernsoul.com/recipes/southern-classics","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Southern American cuisine","links":[["Ambrosia (fruit salad)","dish/ambrosia-fruit-salad"],["Barbecue bologna","dish/barbecue-bologna"],["Chess pie","dish/chess-pie"],["Chicken Maryland","dish/chicken-maryland"],["Chitlins","dish/chitlins"],["Conecuh Sausage","dish/conecuh-sausage"],["Grape hull pie","dish/grape-hull-pie"],["Lemon pepper wings","dish/lemon-pepper-wings"],["Mississippi mud pie","dish/mississippi-mud-pie"],["Monroe Sausage","dish/monroe-sausage"],["Moon Pie","dish/moon-pie"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/e/ed/Plate_of_food_at_Maurice%27s_Gourmet_BBQ.jpg/500px-Plate_of_food_at_Maurice%27s_Gourmet_BBQ.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Nathan Cardozo","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creat